\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces FlowA architecture. The adapter layer wraps five frozen checkpoints without modifying vendored code; the algorithm layer exposes the four-port control surface and the thirteen scheduler families; the evaluation layer supplies model-agnostic metrics and diagnostics. All three layers rest on a shared framework kernel that carries the typed state bundles and the SHA-256 hash-chained ledger used for byte-stable replay. Dependency direction is adapter~$\to $~algorithm, adapter~$\to $~eval, and algorithm/eval~$\to $~framework.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flowa-architecture}{{2}{4}{FlowA architecture. The adapter layer wraps five frozen checkpoints without modifying vendored code; the algorithm layer exposes the four-port control surface and the thirteen scheduler families; the evaluation layer supplies model-agnostic metrics and diagnostics. All three layers rest on a shared framework kernel that carries the typed state bundles and the SHA-256 hash-chained ledger used for byte-stable replay. Dependency direction is adapter~$\to $~algorithm, adapter~$\to $~eval, and algorithm/eval~$\to $~framework}{figure.2}{}}
