\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Evidence comparison across the eleven headline cells. (a) Per-cell standardized effect size $|d|$ on a log scale; the dashed line marks the $|d|=0.8$ STRONG-promotion bar. R6 contributes two points (live scPerplexity and hard-tier pLDDT). (b) The eleven-cell verdict distribution (three STRONG $+$ one CONDITIONAL $+$ one TIE $+$ two PARTIAL $+$ four supplementary). R5b is protocol-conditional, R5c is a frontier comparison, and the four K-cells are supplementary; none of them carries a single standardized effect size, so they are omitted from (a). Values are transcribed verbatim from Sec.~VII-B.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
